idents of Chile have issued of shares and other equity into the part held by non-residents, as the country reports it to the OECD, and the rest, held by residents (our calculation: issued minus non-residents), in its own currency and at market value. Non-residents means every holder outside the country, including foreign central banks and funds. It does not say which kind of resident holds the rest, which needs the country's own accounts. Measured the other way, from residents' holdings of every issuer minus their foreign holdings, residents hold 9.4% of the total less than shown here, so Chile's own figures do not fully agree with each other. Chile reports no listed-shares line to the OECD, so this is listed and unlisted shares and other equity together. Source: OECD."}